  faqs: [
    { question: "Is there an IB or IGCSE school in Vedaranyam?", answer: "Not that we could confirm. Town schools follow the Tamil Nadu State Board, Matriculation or CBSE, and the nearest confirmed IB or Cambridge schools lie in Thanjavur district, Madurai and Chennai. A Vedaranyam family that wants either syllabus therefore studies through an online school or a boarding place, and IB Gram teaches alongside whichever route it has chosen." },
    { question: "How do I find an IB tutor for my child in Vedaranyam?", answer: "Write or message us with the programme, subject, level and the exam series your child is aiming at. We then propose a tutor who has taught that precise course, and arrange a free trial lesson at a time that suits your household. If the first match does not feel right, we propose another; nothing is fixed until you have seen a lesson, and that is the whole route to IB and IGCSE tutors in Vedaranyam." },
    { question: "Do you have IGCSE tutors in Vedaranyam for both Cambridge and Pearson Edexcel?", answer: "Yes, both. For Cambridge the match is made on syllabus code and tier, say Chemistry 0620 at Extended, and for Pearson on the specification and on whether the student sits Foundation or Higher. Each lesson uses that board's own past papers and mark schemes, never a generic IGCSE worksheet, and it is delivered online." },
    { question: "Do your tutors visit homes in Vedaranyam?", answer: "No. Home visits run only in Gurugram and parts of Delhi NCR, and no tutor travels to Vedaranyam. Your child still gets a private lesson at home, taught live on a laptop, with the tutor on screen and every worked problem shared. The teaching is one to one; only the walk to the front door is missing." },
    { question: "What does IB or IGCSE tuition cost for a family in Vedaranyam?", answer: "The rate is set by programme and level, subject, session length and how recently the tutor has taught that exact syllabus, and you receive it in writing before the free trial. Diploma Higher Level work generally sits above MYP or IGCSE Core support. There is no price list to compare, and no travel cost is added because every lesson is online." },
    { question: "My child is enrolled in an online international school while we live in Vedaranyam. Can a tutor still help?", answer: "Yes, and small-town families in this position are common. The tutor works alongside the platform your child already uses, chosen for the exact subject and level, and concentrates on the topics where self-paced or recorded teaching is not sinking in. The school keeps its own teaching and assessment; the tutor adds a live person." },
    { question: "My child boards in Thanjavur, Madurai or Chennai. Can tutoring continue during holidays at home?", answer: "Yes. We choose a tutor who has taught the same subject, level and syllabus as your child's boarding school, so a holiday block in Vedaranyam picks up where the term ended. Many families book a heavier run over the summer break and a lighter weekly slot on term-time weekends, with the pace agreed in advance." },
    { question: "Is there a free trial lesson before we commit?", answer: "Yes. Before you pay or agree to anything, the proposed tutor teaches your child one genuine topic from the actual course, online. Afterwards you receive a short written plan for the first month. If you want to go ahead you confirm, and if not, you can ask for a different tutor or simply stop; nothing is owed for the trial." },
    { question: "What happens if a cyclone alert or a power cut interrupts a lesson?", answer: "The lesson is moved. Vedaranyam sits on an exposed stretch of the Palk Strait coast, and the October to December monsoon can bring alerts and outages, so we suggest a charged laptop, a power bank and a second data connection, and we agree in advance how a missed session is made up before exam season." },
    { question: "Can a tutor help with an IB Internal Assessment from Vedaranyam?", answer: "Yes, as a coach and never as an author. A tutor can help your child narrow a topic into a question that can actually be tested, explain how each criterion is awarded, check that the method will produce enough data and respond honestly to a draft. Producing or rewriting any of the assessed text is where support ends, and the work stays the student's own." },
    { question: "Which IB Diploma subjects can you cover for a Vedaranyam student?", answer: "Requests are most often for Maths in either form, Physics, Chemistry, Biology, Economics, Business Management, English A and Computer Science, with Theory of Knowledge and Extended Essay guidance running beside them. Tamil A and Hindi B are possible where your child's programme includes them. Give us the subjects and levels, and we check who has recent experience of that exact course." },
    { question: "Do you teach IB MYP and PYP students, or only the Diploma?", answer: "We teach from the primary years upward. In MYP the work usually centres on writing to a criterion in Sciences and Language and Literature, and on getting the Personal Project started early. PYP lessons are shorter and more frequent, with reading, mental maths and Exhibition research as the main threads." },
    { question: "Does online tutoring work as well as a classroom teacher for IB or IGCSE in Vedaranyam?", answer: "For most students it does, and in a town with no IB or IGCSE school it is also the only workable route. A shared whiteboard, past papers on screen and a worked solution saved for revision let a tutor do nearly everything a specialist would in a room, and the pool of tutors is national instead of limited to whoever lives locally." },
    { question: "Will my child's Tamil-medium schooling make the switch harder?", answer: "It adds one step, not a barrier. The early weeks go into English command words, such as evaluate, justify and discuss, and into writing a structured paragraph, before content gets heavy. Students who are strong in the subject but new to English-medium assessment usually close the gap within a term or two of regular lessons." },
    { question: "When should my child start IB or IGCSE tutoring from Vedaranyam?", answer: "Early is better: ideally at the beginning of Class 11 for the Diploma, or Grade 9 for IGCSE, so that weak foundations are repaired well before coursework deadlines and predicted grades matter. Starting later still works when lessons are narrowed to the topics carrying the most marks and to timed papers under exam conditions." },
    { question: "What if my child and the tutor do not get along?", answer: "Say so and we will introduce someone else. Families hear from us every few weeks in any case, and a change is made whenever the fit is wrong; a child should not have to sit through months of lessons that are not working. The trial lesson exists so that this judgement can be made early and without awkwardness." },
    { question: "Is IB Gram connected to any school, or to the IB, Cambridge or Pearson?", answer: "No. IB Gram is an independent tutoring service. It has no partnership with the schools mentioned on this page, in Vedaranyam, Sengipatti, Madurai or Chennai, and no connection with the International Baccalaureate, Cambridge or Pearson. Schools appear only so a family can see where the options are, and appearing is not a recommendation." },
  ],

